        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_1522"/>
        <dc:title>Risk aware optimization of water sensor placement</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>This paper addresses the identification of optimal &quot;sensing spots&quot;, within a network for monitoring the spread of &quot;effects&quot; triggered by &quot;events&quot;. Many real-world problems fit into this general framework: we focused on the early detection of contamination events in Water Distribution Networks (WDN). We model the sensor placement as a bi-objective optimization problem, aiming at minimizing the mean and standard deviation of detection time over a set of different simulated contamination events and solved using NSGA-II. A problem-specific data structure is proposed enabling a deeper analysis of empirical convergence of the population.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>July 8, 2021</dc:date>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
                <rdf:value>https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3449726.3459477</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted>2026-07-24</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <z:libraryCatalog>ACM Digital Library</z:libraryCatalog>
        <bib:pages>295–296</bib:pages>
    </rdf:Description>
